  RootNode:
    dialogues:
    - Food pantry - night
    - y:Wait, I can take care of the remaining food.
    - "w:I- Sir, you\u2019re the president. Respectfully, we should be doing the
      heavy work."
    - "y:That\u2019s right, I\u2019m the president. So you\u2019ll do as I say, yes?"
    - "w:\u2026Alright."
    - "After the worker leaves, you take a look at the food inside, and unsurprisingly
      it\u2019s the food that had been rerouted."
    - You pack the food in your bag.
    - w:I thought you were going to take care of the food.
    - y:I thought I told you to leave?
    - "w:If I report you, I\u2019ll get a reward."
    - "y:I\u2019m just giving the food to the people it rightfully belongs to."
    - "y:As a labor worker you\u2019re probably not very well off. I can\u2019t blame
      you for wanting that money. But here\u2019s so many people that need help and
      they aren't getting it. I\u2019m just giving it to them. Can\u2019t you at
      least give those people a chance?"
    - ???:Um, mister?
    - You turn around at the familiar voice.
    - y:Clare? What are you doing here?
    - She glances nervously at the food pantry worker.
    - "w:Clare\u2026that name\u2026no way, are you\u2026?"
    - y:What? Do you know her?
    - "w:That must be Sarah\u2019s child\u2026She worked here back then\u2026I knew
      she had a child, but- We couldn\u2019t afford to take in anyone else anymore."
    - Clare does seem to fully understand what the man is saying and walks to hide
      behind you.
    - "y:You don\u2019t need to worry, I\u2019ll take care of her."
    - The worker glances between you and her, then crouches down to her level.
    - w:Hey, Clare, these past few days, have, have you been getting food?
    - Clare quietly nods.
    - c:Mister. Give food.
    - c:Give food to many. Save many.
    - c:I like mister.
    nextDialogue: {fileID: 0}
    bgNum: 1
